This repository is a throughline *source*: a requirements graph, not a program. It
re-expresses PEP 8 (Style Guide for Python Code) and the docstring conventions of
PEP 257 as a grounded IDD graph so consuming projects can compose it with
throughline.

PEP 8 and PEP 257 are published by the Python Software Foundation and their
authors (Guido van Rossum, Barry Warsaw, Alyssa Coghlan, David Goodger, and
contributors) and are placed in the public domain / licensed under the CC0 1.0
and Open Publication License terms that govern the Python Enhancement Proposals.
The rule text re-expressed here in items' `text`/`attrs.source_ref` is derived
from those PEPs; this repository claims no ownership over that content and
reproduces it for interoperability. See https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/ and
https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/ for the authoritative sources.
